Subject: keyring_vault unit test library links ext::curl, like the component itself
Error: unittest/gunit/components/keyring_vault: ../ps-src/components/keyrings/keyring_vault/backend/vault_curl.h:26:10:
  fatal error: curl/curl.h: No such file or directory
Why: the test library (component_keyring_vault_test) compiles the vault backend but never links ext::curl, so
  it only built while curl.h sat in /usr/include (system curl). With WITH_CURL=bundled (OpenSSL ruling,
  docs/deviations.md: Wolfi's curl-dev needs the OpenSSL 4 headers) curl's include dir comes only from ext::curl.
  Build-only fix: the same curl the component links.
Upstream: none found (searched the percona-server tree at the pinned tag)
Drop-when: the test CMakeLists links ext::curl upstream, or the recipe goes back to WITH_CURL=system

--- a/unittest/gunit/components/keyring_vault/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/unittest/gunit/components/keyring_vault/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
 add_library(component_keyring_vault_test STATIC ${SRC_FILES})
 add_dependencies(component_keyring_vault_test GenError)
-target_link_libraries(component_keyring_vault_test extra::rapidjson library_mysys)
+target_link_libraries(component_keyring_vault_test ext::curl extra::rapidjson library_mysys)
 target_compile_definitions(component_keyring_vault_test PUBLIC LOG_COMPONENT_TAG="component_keyring_vault")
 target_include_directories(component_keyring_vault_test SYSTEM PUBLIC
   ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}
